1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:01,470
<i>Sooha.</i>

2
00:00:02,770 --> 00:00:04,330
<i>Sooha, can you hear me?</i>

3
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:06,930
Sooha.

4
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:12,090
<i>Sooha, are you okay? Are you hurt?</i>

5
00:00:12,090 --> 00:00:13,110
Heli?

6
00:00:13,470 --> 00:00:14,380
<i>Where are you?</i>

7
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:15,490
<i>I'll come get you.</i>

8
00:00:15,490 --> 00:00:18,240
<i>Um, I'm busy right now.</i>

9
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:19,870
Huh? Sooha?

10
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,290
Khan!

11
00:00:21,290 --> 00:00:22,610
It's good to see you again.

12
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:24,690
Uh, um...

13
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:26,830
<i>He's gone.</i>

14
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:30,000
<i>He vanished!</i>

15
00:01:54,070 --> 00:02:00,010
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

16
00:02:02,030 --> 00:02:05,020
- Night of the Total Eclipse -

17
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:07,800
Are you alone, or are you with someone?

18
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:08,770
Huh? Um...

19
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:11,710
She's here with me. 
You got a problem with that?

20
00:02:11,710 --> 00:02:12,480
Jakah...

21
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:14,190
It's just the two of you?

22
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:16,040
No, the others came with—

23
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:17,740
That's none of your business.

24
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,430
Khan!

25
00:02:20,430 --> 00:02:22,320
Let's race boats!

26
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:24,160
Hey, it's Sooha!

27
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:25,180
Good to see...

28
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,770
Sooha! Jakah!

29
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:28,860
Shion!

30
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:29,960
Are you two...

31
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:30,900
Huh?

32
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:32,730
Sooha.

33
00:02:32,730 --> 00:02:33,720
Heli.

34
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,100
Are you hurt anywhere?

35
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:36,710
No, I'm fine.

36
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:38,720
The others saved me.

37
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:48,870
Hurt? Did something happen?

38
00:02:49,390 --> 00:02:52,690
Some vampires showed up 
out of nowhere just now.

39
00:02:52,690 --> 00:02:53,810
What?!

40
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:56,580
At this hour? And in the plaza?

41
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:58,360
Where are they now?

42
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:00,550
We dealt with them.

43
00:03:00,550 --> 00:03:02,870
You don't have to worry about it.

44
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:04,060
You can't be serious.

45
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:08,230
We wouldn't have put Sooha 
in danger in the first place.

46
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:09,520
What was that?!

47
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:10,540
Jaan.

48
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:14,100
Sooha, don't get too close to these guys.

49
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:15,810
For your own sake.

50
00:03:15,810 --> 00:03:16,460
Huh?

51
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:20,220
That's right. You should hang 
out with us next weekend.

52
00:03:20,990 --> 00:03:24,130
Sooha already agreed to hang 
out with us next weekend.

53
00:03:24,130 --> 00:03:25,600
What? I did?

54
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:29,470
I see. Then let's meet up 
the weekend after that!

55
00:03:29,470 --> 00:03:29,930
Huh?

56
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:34,180
We have plans that weekend 
and every weekend after.

57
00:03:34,180 --> 00:03:38,100
Forever and ever, never-ending!

58
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:40,570
Quit messing with me, brat!

59
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:42,350
What was that, idiot?!

60
00:03:42,350 --> 00:03:45,370
Shut up! Takes one to know one!

61
00:03:49,310 --> 00:03:53,690
Anyway, Sooha, we really are throwing 
a birthday party three weeks from now.

62
00:03:53,690 --> 00:03:54,830
You'll come, right?

63
00:03:54,830 --> 00:03:58,100
Huh? I-If it's someone's birthday, 
I'll definitely be there.

64
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:00,090
Hey! Don't lie to her!

65
00:04:00,090 --> 00:04:01,560
It's true.

66
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:04,130
If you don't believe me, 
why don't you come, too?

67
00:04:04,130 --> 00:04:05,350
Like hell I'm going!

68
00:04:05,350 --> 00:04:07,430
I'm not celebrating that!

69
00:04:07,430 --> 00:04:10,810
I'm joking. I'd never invite you guys.

70
00:04:10,810 --> 00:04:14,650
I think it'd be nice to
 celebrate together.

71
00:04:14,650 --> 00:04:16,680
If Sooha says so, then I'm going for sure.

72
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:19,530
Me, too. Send me an invitation.

73
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:20,930
I'd like to go, too.

74
00:04:20,930 --> 00:04:21,690
What?!

75
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:23,580
I said I was joking!

76
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:25,790
There's no way I'd ever invite you guys.

77
00:04:25,790 --> 00:04:26,660
What was that?!

78
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:30,270
We're offering to attend 
your boring little party!

79
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,620
That's enough.

80
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:34,290
You dusty losers aren't invited.

81
00:04:34,290 --> 00:04:36,040
Quit it, guys.

82
00:04:38,810 --> 00:04:42,210
Sooha said she was attacked 
by vampires, right?

83
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:46,140
They put Sooha in danger.

84
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:47,180
Yeah.

85
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:50,610
You two seem awfully
 concerned about Sooha.

86
00:04:50,610 --> 00:04:54,180
Huh? Oh, yeah. I wonder why.

87
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:58,300
I sense a strange power in her.

88
00:04:58,930 --> 00:05:00,970
To tell you the truth, so do I.

89
00:05:00,970 --> 00:05:01,690
No!

90
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:06,820
Sooha's words froze me in place then.

91
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:09,820
There's something up with her.

92
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:13,450
Maybe it's related to 
today's vampire attack.

93
00:05:13,450 --> 00:05:16,170
Yeah, and that's not all.

94
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:18,860
They may have been protecting Sooha,

95
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:22,800
but I'm intrigued that they 
fought their own kind.

96
00:05:29,090 --> 00:05:31,600
<i>That person I saw at the plaza today...</i>

97
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:36,280
<i>If Chris had lived to be an adult, 
he definitely would've looked like that.</i>

98
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:44,900
But I thought Chris was dead.

99
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:48,130
Sooha.

100
00:05:48,530 --> 00:05:52,190
<i>He definitely called my name back there.</i>

101
00:05:52,610 --> 00:05:55,310
<i>Is Chris actually still alive?</i>

102
00:05:55,630 --> 00:05:58,060
<i>But how?</i>

103
00:05:58,060 --> 00:06:02,060
<i>And why didn't he come see me sooner?</i>

104
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:04,710
<i>I can't believe he 
disappeared right away, too.</i>

105
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:08,220
<i>No, none of that matters!</i>

106
00:06:08,690 --> 00:06:10,970
<i>I only care that you're still alive!</i>

107
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:33,330
Chris!

108
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:38,790
Chris!

109
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:41,960
Chris! Chris!

110
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:44,880
Sooha, I missed you.

111
00:06:45,170 --> 00:06:46,340
You're alive?

112
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:48,090
Yeah, I am.

113
00:06:48,430 --> 00:06:50,940
Are you really Chris?

114
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:53,890
Yes, really. This brings back memories.

115
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:57,310
Anyway, you haven't changed a bit.

116
00:06:58,890 --> 00:06:59,970
Chris...

117
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:04,310
You really are Chris!

118
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:09,810
I'm glad to see you again, Sooha.

119
00:07:13,730 --> 00:07:14,850
Chris...

120
00:07:15,350 --> 00:07:17,260
But why?

121
00:07:25,610 --> 00:07:26,810
<i>A dream?</i>

122
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:30,010
<i>That must've been a dream.</i>

123
00:07:33,950 --> 00:07:35,080
<i>I know.</i>

124
00:07:36,510 --> 00:07:38,600
<i>There's no way Chris will be there.</i>

125
00:07:39,020 --> 00:07:41,630
<i>This is all a dream.</i>

126
00:07:53,390 --> 00:07:56,780
I knew it. He's not here.

127
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:04,290
Why is it so dark when
 there's a full moon tonight?

128
00:08:26,070 --> 00:08:29,980
<i>I'm the only one who 
didn't transform again.</i>

129
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:34,550
<i>Why am I the only one who can't?</i>

130
00:08:41,690 --> 00:08:47,130
<i>Everyone else naturally becomes a wolf 
under the light of the full moon,</i>

131
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,930
<i>so why not me?</i>

132
00:08:51,170 --> 00:08:54,570
<i>Am I defective after all?</i>

133
00:09:10,790 --> 00:09:11,700
Sooha?

134
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:13,690
Khan?

135
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:37,460
Khan.

136
00:09:44,470 --> 00:09:46,760
What are you doing here at this hour?

137
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:48,240
<i>And in pajamas?</i>

138
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:50,230
<i>Huh? What?</i>

139
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:53,550
<i>He seems different from usual.</i>

140
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:57,010
I-I was in such a hurry, I didn't change!

141
00:09:57,010 --> 00:09:58,690
D-Don't worry about it.

142
00:09:58,690 --> 00:10:00,700
It happens when you're rushing.

143
00:10:01,130 --> 00:10:02,690
Heck, it happens to me all the time.

144
00:10:02,690 --> 00:10:04,570
What? All the time?

145
00:10:06,310 --> 00:10:09,030
A-Anyway, what are you doing here?

146
00:10:09,030 --> 00:10:09,790
Huh?

147
00:10:09,790 --> 00:10:13,960
Oh, um... I-I just wanted 
to see the ocean at night.

148
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:15,210
By yourself?

149
00:10:15,210 --> 00:10:18,910
Yeah. I thought there was
 a full moon tonight.

150
00:10:21,140 --> 00:10:22,590
It's a total eclipse.

151
00:10:22,970 --> 00:10:30,020
When the Sun, Earth, and Moon line up,
 the Moon is hidden in the Earth's shadow.

152
00:10:30,650 --> 00:10:32,420
It's a really special day.

153
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:38,300
Yeah. I learned about it, 
but this is my first time seeing it.

154
00:10:39,450 --> 00:10:41,100
By the way...

155
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:44,340
What are you doing here at this hour?

156
00:10:44,340 --> 00:10:47,690
I... came to see the total eclipse.

157
00:10:47,690 --> 00:10:49,040
I see.

158
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:51,540
By yourself? Where are the others?

159
00:10:52,210 --> 00:10:54,520
It's just me. They're...

160
00:10:57,300 --> 00:10:58,350
asleep.

161
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:03,980
L-Listen, Sooha. Want me to walk you back?

162
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:04,640
Huh?

163
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:08,480
Some vampires showed up 
today, right? I'm worried.

164
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:10,730
Are you sure? Thanks.

165
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:13,480
I was actually a little scared.

166
00:11:13,930 --> 00:11:17,000
About the vampires, 
and about the stray dogs, too.

167
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,020
Stray dogs?

168
00:11:18,020 --> 00:11:21,770
Yeah. Didn't you hear
 them howling just now?

169
00:11:21,770 --> 00:11:23,560
W-Were they?

170
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:25,720
I hope they don't attack people.

171
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:28,470
They don't! Especially not wolves.

172
00:11:28,470 --> 00:11:28,940
What?

173
00:11:28,940 --> 00:11:30,390
Uh, I mean...

174
00:11:30,570 --> 00:11:34,360
They're, uh... surprisingly kind animals.

175
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:38,060
That's true. Plus, wolves are cool.

176
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:40,480
What? You really think so?

177
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:42,410
You like wolves, too?

178
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:45,180
Yeah! At least, I like seeing them on TV.

179
00:11:45,630 --> 00:11:49,020
But I'd be scared if I ran into one.

180
00:11:49,390 --> 00:11:50,460
I see.

181
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:53,790
W-Well, I'll walk you back.

182
00:11:53,790 --> 00:11:55,620
Okay. Thanks.

183
00:12:04,950 --> 00:12:09,040
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

184
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:13,040
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

185
00:12:16,030 --> 00:12:18,670
Jino, do you have any plans for today?

186
00:12:19,410 --> 00:12:20,550
Not really.

187
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:23,030
How do you feel?

188
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,150
Normal?

189
00:12:29,810 --> 00:12:31,590
<i>Stare...</i>

190
00:12:31,590 --> 00:12:35,330
You want me to practice shooting 
with you, right? I know.

191
00:12:38,090 --> 00:12:40,810
You never stop throwing balls around.

192
00:12:40,810 --> 00:12:41,670
Hey.

193
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:44,650
Huh? He's not with you?

194
00:12:45,530 --> 00:12:47,480
Well, Shion said...

195
00:12:48,570 --> 00:12:49,590
Shion.

196
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:52,580
I'm so tired.

197
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:53,620
What's up?

198
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:56,080
I didn't get to see Sooha.

199
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:58,390
Oh, right. The birthday party.

200
00:12:58,390 --> 00:13:01,750
There's no rush. 
You'll see her eventually, right?

201
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:04,490
I couldn't wait to give this to her.

202
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:06,800
I wore myself out looking
 everywhere for her.

203
00:13:07,130 --> 00:13:09,580
Yes, yes. That must've been hard for you.

204
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:13,700
Since you're so tired, 
I'll give this to Sooha for you.

205
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:14,520
Hey.

206
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:16,190
Don't, Jaan.

207
00:13:16,730 --> 00:13:18,220
I'll give it to her.

208
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:18,810
Jino?

209
00:13:18,810 --> 00:13:20,600
If you're gonna fight, I'll do it.

210
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,400
Noa?

211
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:25,240
I'm concerned about your 
ability to deliver the invite.

212
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,950
Maybe I should do it.

213
00:13:26,950 --> 00:13:28,800
You too, Jakah?!

214
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:29,740
Here.

215
00:13:29,990 --> 00:13:32,250
Honestly, guys!

216
00:13:32,250 --> 00:13:32,850
Sorry.

217
00:13:32,850 --> 00:13:33,870
Sorry, sorry.

218
00:13:33,870 --> 00:13:36,420
It's strange, isn't it?

219
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:45,510
Before we met Sooha, we always 
wanted to keep to ourselves.

220
00:13:45,510 --> 00:13:46,860
You're right.

221
00:13:47,190 --> 00:13:49,770
We'd never thought about
 inviting someone else.

222
00:13:49,770 --> 00:13:51,720
I'm excited for the party.

223
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:55,560
All the more reason to make 
sure she gets the invitation.

224
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:57,350
I know.

225
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:02,150
I think I know where Sooha might be.

226
00:14:07,070 --> 00:14:08,040
Sooha.

227
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:11,460
Heli.

228
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:12,790
Here to borrow some books?

229
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:14,430
Yeah. What about you?

230
00:14:14,430 --> 00:14:15,750
I'm returning a book today.

231
00:14:16,570 --> 00:14:18,230
That's the book from the other day.

232
00:14:18,230 --> 00:14:20,690
Yeah. I finished it.

233
00:14:20,690 --> 00:14:21,880
Was it interesting?

234
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:26,190
Yeah. It's on legends from
 an ancient kingdom.

235
00:14:26,690 --> 00:14:29,090
There are vampires and werewolves in them.

236
00:14:29,090 --> 00:14:31,390
Vampires and werewolves...

237
00:14:31,390 --> 00:14:34,610
They're famous for being
 ancient mortal enemies.

238
00:14:34,610 --> 00:14:36,820
They often appear together.

239
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:38,990
I see.

240
00:14:39,630 --> 00:14:43,480
Werewolves turn into wolves 
during the full moon, right?

241
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:44,750
That's right.

242
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:48,540
Come to think of it, there was 
a total eclipse yesterday.

243
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:49,250
Yeah.

244
00:14:49,730 --> 00:14:55,780
Maybe they can't transform during a full
 moon if a total eclipse conceals it.

245
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:58,010
I'm not sure.

246
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:01,670
But apparently, werewolves fall in love

247
00:15:01,670 --> 00:15:04,540
with the first woman they 
see during a total eclipse,

248
00:15:04,930 --> 00:15:08,130
and will love that woman alone
for the rest of their life.

249
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:10,430
That sounds lovely.

250
00:15:10,430 --> 00:15:13,510
But eclipses are rare.

251
00:15:13,510 --> 00:15:16,980
I doubt they fall in love that way often.

252
00:15:16,980 --> 00:15:19,920
That's true. Did you see the eclipse?

253
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:22,610
No. I was asleep.

254
00:15:22,610 --> 00:15:23,830
Did you?

255
00:15:23,830 --> 00:15:26,270
Yeah, at the inlet.

256
00:15:26,270 --> 00:15:30,240
What? You went to
 the inlet after that? Why?

257
00:15:31,230 --> 00:15:33,560
I just wanted to see the ocean at night.

258
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:38,850
I thought there was a full moon last night 
and was surprised by how dark it was,

259
00:15:38,850 --> 00:15:41,790
and then Khan told me 
about the total eclipse.

260
00:15:43,650 --> 00:15:45,590
We happened to meet by the sea.

261
00:15:45,890 --> 00:15:49,340
You met Khan on the night
 of a total eclipse?

262
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:52,840
Yeah. What about it?

263
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:55,020
Oh, it's nothing.

264
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:56,860
Invite me next time.

265
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:57,660
Okay.

266
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:00,670
<i>A shadow crossed his face for a moment.</i>

267
00:16:00,670 --> 00:16:03,940
<i>Did he not like that I met up with Khan?</i>

268
00:16:04,330 --> 00:16:07,010
I like looking at the sea at night, too.

269
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:08,940
Really?

270
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:12,660
<i>Come to think of it, I wonder 
why they don't get along.</i>

271
00:16:12,660 --> 00:16:14,700
<i>Is it because they attend rival schools?</i>

272
00:16:15,950 --> 00:16:20,150
<i>They said they compete for the 
nightball championship every year.</i>

273
00:16:21,670 --> 00:16:25,030
<i>Maybe they're on edge since 
they have a game coming up.</i>

274
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:26,920
<i>Well, that can't be helped.</i>

275
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:29,490
Anyway, yesterday must've been tough.

276
00:16:29,490 --> 00:16:31,960
Huh? Oh, yeah.

277
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:36,380
Let me know right away if 
anything unusual happens, okay?

278
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:40,970
This wasn't just a coincidence.

279
00:16:40,970 --> 00:16:43,230
They were targeting Sooha.

280
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:48,860
Okay. I'm fine, though.

281
00:16:49,220 --> 00:16:51,810
So, have you gotten used to school?

282
00:16:51,810 --> 00:16:56,260
Yeah. For the first time in my life, 
I think I'm having fun at school.

283
00:16:57,370 --> 00:16:58,490
I see.

284
00:16:58,890 --> 00:17:01,750
All because of you, Heli. Thank you.

285
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:03,170
You don't need to thank me.

286
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:06,250
I'm just glad you're having fun.

287
00:17:06,250 --> 00:17:09,520
But you're the reason I made friends with—

288
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:10,410
Sooha.

289
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:11,960
Jino.

290
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,350
So you were at the library after all.

291
00:17:14,350 --> 00:17:16,050
Are you both borrowing books?

292
00:17:16,050 --> 00:17:18,590
Yeah. Heli's returning one, actually.

293
00:17:18,590 --> 00:17:20,160
Ah, I see.

294
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,930
Are you all borrowing books, too?

295
00:17:21,930 --> 00:17:25,780
Of course we are. Reading's my hobby.

296
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:29,410
I came to borrow a book 
on quantum mechanics.

297
00:17:29,410 --> 00:17:31,380
I've been interested in it lately.

298
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:33,280
Stop lying, you two.

299
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:36,350
Noa, your book's upside down.

300
00:17:39,170 --> 00:17:41,820
We just thought you'd be here, Sooha.

301
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:45,160
Aside from Heli, 
none of us really read much.

302
00:17:45,830 --> 00:17:47,490
Don't tell her that.

303
00:17:48,090 --> 00:17:50,090
I read three whole lines.

304
00:17:50,370 --> 00:17:52,690
So, what were you talking about?

305
00:17:53,710 --> 00:17:56,300
I was asking Heli about the book he read.

306
00:17:56,530 --> 00:17:59,430
He said it was about an ancient kingdom.

307
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:01,850
There are werewolves and 
vampires in the stories.

308
00:18:01,850 --> 00:18:02,770
Werewolves?

309
00:18:03,430 --> 00:18:07,860
Yeah. Heli told me about 
a romantic werewolf legend.

310
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:08,600
What legend?

311
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:13,850
During a total eclipse, werewolves fall 
in love with the first woman they see.

312
00:18:13,850 --> 00:18:16,110
They love her and only her forever.

313
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:18,840
Isn't that so romantic?

314
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:22,490
Oh, please.

315
00:18:22,490 --> 00:18:26,500
Maybe so, but werewolves are just mutts.

316
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:30,010
Yeah. You have to deal with the 
shedding whenever they're around.

317
00:18:30,010 --> 00:18:31,790
And you'll never stop sneezing.

318
00:18:32,340 --> 00:18:37,470
They say they're part-human and part-wolf, 
but they're less than 10% human.

319
00:18:37,470 --> 00:18:38,590
Yeah.

320
00:18:40,970 --> 00:18:43,780
Oh, Solon? You're here?

321
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:51,020
Y-Yeah. Anyone who's half-stray dog
 is savage, stupid, and crude.

322
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:54,350
Now, now. No need to go that far.

323
00:18:54,350 --> 00:18:57,240
Sooha thinks the werewolf 
legend is romantic.

324
00:18:57,580 --> 00:19:01,450
About them falling in love with the first 
person they see during a total eclipse?

325
00:19:01,450 --> 00:19:03,720
That's just werewolves being stupid.

326
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:06,870
Vampires are far... better.

327
00:19:06,870 --> 00:19:08,040
But...

328
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:12,680
Vampires don't feel any love at all.

329
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:17,150
No, they don't even have 
the kind heart of a human.

330
00:19:17,570 --> 00:19:21,470
Just yesterday, they suddenly attacked me!

331
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:24,090
And... and...

332
00:19:24,090 --> 00:19:28,190
they kill innocent people 
and turn them into vampires!

333
00:19:28,930 --> 00:19:32,100
So there's no way they
 even know what love is.

334
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:35,690
Vampires are just cold, brutal monsters!

335
00:19:35,690 --> 00:19:38,230
Werewolves are way better!

336
00:19:38,230 --> 00:19:40,820
No, you can't even compare them.

337
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:43,340
Vampires are the worst!

338
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:51,910
S-Sorry for flipping out so suddenly.

339
00:19:51,910 --> 00:19:54,080
I-It's fine.

340
00:19:54,370 --> 00:19:56,870
We shouldn't have said 
those things to begin with.

341
00:19:57,340 --> 00:19:59,090
Y-Yeah.

342
00:19:59,090 --> 00:20:01,470
You have nothing to apologize for, Sooha.

343
00:20:01,470 --> 00:20:02,580
Yeah.

344
00:20:02,930 --> 00:20:04,620
Everyone has their own preferences.

345
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:05,620
Yeah.

346
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:10,330
I just really hate vampires.

347
00:20:10,330 --> 00:20:11,020
Yeah.

348
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:16,860
We know. Everyone hates vampires.

349
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:27,410
I see. Her friend was killed by a vampire.

350
00:20:27,410 --> 00:20:29,990
Yeah. That's why she hates them so much.

351
00:20:30,250 --> 00:20:31,650
That's not all.

352
00:20:32,190 --> 00:20:34,790
You know that incredible power she has?

353
00:20:34,790 --> 00:20:36,270
You mean her super strength?

354
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:39,720
She's been mistaken for 
a vampire because of it.

355
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:42,610
She's probably suffered a lot for it.

356
00:20:43,850 --> 00:20:46,190
Then what are we supposed to do?

357
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:50,640
I couldn't give this to her.

358
00:20:50,950 --> 00:20:53,270
Not even you could do it?

359
00:20:53,270 --> 00:20:56,850
What? I know how to read a room, okay?

360
00:20:56,850 --> 00:21:00,610
Maybe we can't invite her
 to our birthday party.

361
00:21:26,870 --> 00:21:31,260
<i>I thought there was a full moon last night 
and was surprised by how dark it was,</i>

362
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:34,460
<i>and then Khan told me 
about the total eclipse.</i>

363
00:21:51,590 --> 00:21:54,010
I finally found you.

364
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:39,510
<i>Next time, Episode 5: 
"Waxing Moon: Bite My Neck."</i>

365
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:40,250
- Bite My Neck -

